program rope_tool
arg nope
status 1
output
Error: unknown command: nope
rope_tool [options] command arguments...

Command-line demo of Ropes: each subcommand builds one or two ropes from its string arguments and prints the result of one Ropes operation.

-h, --help                    Display this help message and exit.

cat A B  Print the concatenation of A and B.


len S  Print the length of S.


fetch S I  Print the character of S at index I (1-based).


slice S LOW HIGH  Print the slice of S from LOW through HIGH, inclusive (1-based).


insert S BEFORE INS  Print S with INS inserted before index BEFORE (1-based).


delete S FROM THROUGH  Print S with FROM through THROUGH removed, inclusive (1-based).


cmp A B  Print -1, 0 or 1: how A compares to B.


index S PATTERN FROM  Print the index of PATTERN in S at or after FROM (1-based), or 0.


rindex S PATTERN FROM  Print the index of the last PATTERN in S at or before FROM (1-based), or 0.


indexchar S CH FROM  Print the index of CH in S at or after FROM (1-based), or 0.


rindexchar S CH FROM  Print the index of CH in S at or before FROM (1-based), or 0.


split S SEP  Print each piece of S split on SEP, one per line.


chars S  Print each character of S, one per line ("for Ch of S loop").


trim S  Print S with leading and trailing whitespace removed.


triml S  Print S with leading whitespace removed.


trimr S  Print S with trailing whitespace removed.


upper S  Print S with ASCII letters uppercased.


lower S  Print S with ASCII letters lowercased.


capitalize S  Print S with its first character uppercased (ASCII only).


uncapitalize S  Print S with its first character lowercased (ASCII only).


repeat S N  Print N concatenated copies of S.


make LEN CH  Print a rope of LEN copies of CH.


bigcat N1 CH1 N2 CH2  Print the length of N1 copies of CH1 concatenated with N2 copies of CH2.


contains S CH FROM  Print TRUE or FALSE: whether CH occurs in S at or after FROM.


escaped S  Print S with special and non-printable characters escaped.


overwrite S POS NEW  Print S with NEW overwriting it starting at index POS (1-based).


head S COUNT  Print the first COUNT characters of S, space-padded if S is shorter.


tail S COUNT  Print the last COUNT characters of S, space-padded if S is shorter.


lines FILE  Read FILE (standard input if FILE is -) and print each line's length, a space, and the line.


readfile FILE  Read all of FILE, byte for byte, and print its length, a space, and its contents escaped.


copyslice S LOW HIGH T POS  Print T with S's characters LOW through HIGH (1-based, inclusive) copied into it at POS.


replaceslice S LOW HIGH BY  Print S with its characters LOW through HIGH (1-based, inclusive) replaced by BY.


count S PATTERN  Print the number of nonoverlapping occurrences of PATTERN in S.


countset S CHARS  Print the number of characters of S that are any of CHARS.


indexset S CHARS FROM  Print the index of the first character at or after FROM in S that is any of CHARS, or 0.


rindexset S CHARS FROM  Print the index of the last character at or before FROM in S that is any of CHARS, or 0.


nonblank S FROM  Print the index of the first non-space character at or after FROM in S, or 0.


rnonblank S FROM  Print the index of the last non-space character at or before FROM in S, or 0.


findtoken S CHARS FROM  Print FIRST LAST: the first run of characters that are any of CHARS, at or after FROM in S.


translate S FROM TO  Print S with each character in FROM replaced by the one at the same place in TO.

